{"author":{"id":"f1a240db6c4c65e230308d533cb7984bde7132e0893983e24a30951c434ff6fe"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1794394199,"nonce":"T9itjSetSz60JNdHP4z1Ogvf1UM=","title":"macOS blocks unsigned release binaries installed as casks","message":"The v1.1.0 igittigit cask installs successfully after placing its definition under Casks/, but running the installed binary on macOS exits with signal 9. The binary has com.apple.quarantine and only an ad-hoc signature; codesign verification passes while spctl rejects it. Local go install works. README documents local Go installation for personal use. No quarantine bypass or signing configuration was authorized. Public macOS binary distribution would require a separate signing/notarization decision.","files":null}]}